            <ArticleTitle>Parosteal osteosarcoma of the cervical vertebra in a dog.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>120-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old Maltese terrier was evaluated for progressive tetraparesis and neck pain. On radiographs, there was a periosteal reaction involving the fourth cervical vertebra. Myelographically, there was extradural compression of the spinal cord associated with the lesion. The dog was euthanized and necropsied. Histopathologic diagnosis was parosteal osteosarcoma of the vertebra.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
